  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Ensure 81% Coverage of LLINs in Vanuatu - Oceania - Multicountry Western Pacific (01-Jan-2018-31-Dec-2020)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multicountry Western Pacific, Malaria, United Nations Development Programme (UNDP Pacific Office in Fiji)This program has the following goals: By the end of 2020, to reduce the annual parasite incidence rate to &lt; 1 per 1,000 nationally and maintain zero confirmed deaths from malaria..  By the end of 2018, to reduce the annual parasite incidence rate to &lt; 2.5 per 1,000 nationally and reduce the annual parasite incidence rate to &lt; 1 per 1,000 in one additional province (Torba) and maintain zero confirmed deaths from malaria.. The objectives of this program are: To sustain 81% coverage with LLINs for the whole population of Vanuatu and accelerate reduction in malaria transmission in selected areas.</narrative>
  </description>
